From: daveey <daveey@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Wed, 18 Nov 2026 22:33:47 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] [daveey] Recover sidebar freshness after gateway probe
 failure

Schedule the existing stale-owner backoff after gateway-unavailable invalidation.
Only an authoritative successful list restores freshness; cached rows stay
fail-closed. Replace the old no-retry expectation with real hook coverage of
15/30/60/60-second retry timing, persistent failure, other-owner isolation,
successful list restoration and stopping retries.

Five whys (bounded by checked evidence):
1. Why did an idle done session lose its stripe? Coordinator-read desktop.log
   for 20261111_090650_1247e7 shows done->none, idle, source=cache,
   outcome=done at 2026-11-18 13:29:29 -08:00, without task/background/
   delegation work; list-refetch restored none->done at 13:33:53.
2. Why could a cached row hide done? offline_cached intentionally suppresses
   authoritative outcome presentation. Keep that fail-closed behavior.
3. Why could freshness remain stale? A gateway-unavailable status observation
   invalidates the owner; status success alone cannot validate session rows.
   A later 13:40:55 log explicitly records gateway-unavailable freshness.
4. Why was recovery delayed until an unrelated refresh? That producer excluded
   probe failures from listStaleOwners, so the existing retry loop had no owner
   eligible to re-list. Add the gateway wildcard to the set.
5. Why was it not caught? Store tests checked invalidation and the hook suite
   explicitly expected no probe-triggered retry, not eventual recovery.

The reported 14.9-second main-process stall is not independently established
as the historical cause of these transitions; no such causal claim is needed
for the reproduced missing-retry defect.

Validation on pool worker with separate dependency tree:
- RED: recovered store regression and new real-hook regression fail on base
  f8107900412daeae725492d4aa8661d0a8ef8404 (empty stale-owner eligibility).
- GREEN: offline-sessions + use-session-list-actions: 105 tests pass.
- Consumers including boot-snapshot, hub-sync, offline owners/actions,
  sidebar fallback/actions and session actions: 13 files, 300 tests pass.
- Desktop tsc --noEmit passes with 3 GiB heap (1.5 GiB trial exhausted heap).

Live Desktop deployment and idle proof remain with parent t_0ac5797a398e994e.
